ll,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097966,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2025-03-29T22:12:31Z","updated_at":"2025-03-30T11:15:25Z","closed_at":"2025-03-30T11:11:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nGodot 4.1.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10\n\n### Issue description\n\nNot sure if intentional, I couldn't find other issues or mentions to this in the documentation. When a node is set to process_mode = ALWAYS, it doesn't receive the `NOTIFICATION_PAUSED` and `NOTIFICATION_UNPAUSED` notifications anymore.\n\nHere's a gif of the MRP attached below:\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fe24f4c4-f8ad-429f-86df-15116d2ea4e0)\n\nWhy would someone want to react to those notifications if setting the node to process_mode = ALWAYS? To change behaviour of the node depending if the tree is paused or not. For example, in my case I have a global audio manager with a sound that is playing always, even when the game is paused, but I want to reduce the volume when pausing.\n\nThis could be related to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/83160, my MRP proves that one too.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Set a node as process_mode = ALWAYS\n- attach a script to the node\n- implement virtual method `func _notification(what: int) -> void` and try to react to the `NOTIFICATION_PAUSED` or `NOTIFICATION_UNPAUSED` notifications\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mrp_notifications_paused_unpaused.zip](http